# Locks the ReadPersonality path in both its forms: PersonalityFile (a file name)
# and the Personality combo (an alias from basic.ini).
#
# Each load must change the search that follows it -- different nodes, score and
# pv from the default personality and from each other. That is the whole point of
# personalities, and it is easy to lose silently: ParseSetoption ignores a command
# it does not recognise and matches the combo value with strcmp, so a malformed or
# mis-cased line is a no-op the engine never complains about. Both mistakes were
# in this transcript until 2026-07-25 -- `PersonalityFile cloe.txt` without the
# `value` keyword, and `Personality value tal` against the alias `Tal` -- which is
# how "a personality load does not affect the eval" came to be written down as an
# upstream quirk. It never was one.
#
# UseBook is off because book moves are time-seeded random; with it off, the
# evaluation is the only thing a personality can still change here.
setoption name Threads value 1
setoption name UseBook value false
setoption name PersonalityFile value cloe.txt
position fen r3r1k1/2p2ppp/p1p1bn2/8/1q2P3/2NPQN2/PPP3PP/R4RK1 b - - 2 15
go depth 12
setoption name Personality value Tal
go depth 12
quit
